   "start": 0.32,
   "text": "Trypsin and chymotrypsin cut proteins into polypeptides. Carboxypeptidase clips amino acids off the carboxyl end, and elastase digests elastin fibers. Only a small fraction becomes free amino acids in the lumen. Most ends up as dipeptides and tripeptides, which peptidases on and inside the enterocytes finish off."
  }
 ],
 "text": "Trypsin and chymotrypsin cut proteins into polypeptides. Carboxypeptidase clips amino acids off the carboxyl end, and elastase digests elastin fibers. Only a small fraction becomes free amino acids in the lumen. Most ends up as dipeptides and tripeptides, which peptidases on and inside the enterocytes finish off."
